WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.348
Somewhere on your machine are thousands of folders.

2
00:00:03.348 --> 00:00:05.601
Everything you ever started.

3
00:00:06.321 --> 00:00:08.573
Innernet turns them into a web of your

4
00:00:08.573 --> 00:00:11.011
own. A search engine,

5
00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.974
and an encyclopedia.

6
00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:16.132
Private, and entirely yours.

7
00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:21.367
It starts with a crawl.

8
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.944
The indexer walks six levels deep,

9
00:00:23.944 --> 00:00:26.022
and quietly skips the noise:

10
00:00:26.022 --> 00:00:30.249
dependencies, builds, caches.

11
00:00:30.969 --> 00:00:32.931
From each folder it reads only a few

12
00:00:32.931 --> 00:00:34.742
things: the README,

13
00:00:34.742 --> 00:00:36.008
the package file,

14
00:00:36.008 --> 00:00:37.320
the git history,

15
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.108
notes for agents.

16
00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.151
Never your secrets.

17
00:00:41.186 --> 00:00:43.287
Key files stay closed,

18
00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:46.028
and passwords are blacked out.

19
00:00:46.748 --> 00:00:47.688
In under a minute,

20
00:00:47.688 --> 00:00:50.847
it all becomes one small index.

21
00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.413
And all of it stays here.

22
00:00:53.413 --> 00:00:54.783
The index, the search,

23
00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:57.012
every page lives on your machine,

24
00:00:57.012 --> 00:00:58.742
and nothing, ever,

25
00:00:58.742 --> 00:01:01.331
is sent away.

26
00:01:02.851 --> 00:01:04.558
Two readers share it.

27
00:01:04.558 --> 00:01:06.369
Search finds anything you type,

28
00:01:06.369 --> 00:01:08.575
in a few milliseconds.

29
00:01:09.295 --> 00:01:12.023
And Innerpedia gives every project an article,

30
00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:14.230
written from what is inside it.

31
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.784
Even namesakes are handled.

32
00:01:16.784 --> 00:01:19.455
Two hundred and four folders called src,

33
00:01:19.455 --> 00:01:21.417
one tidy page.

34
00:01:25.887 --> 00:01:28.604
Every folder is already a site.

35
00:01:28.604 --> 00:01:31.704
A little care makes it a great one.

36
00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:34.073
Start with a README.

37
00:01:34.073 --> 00:01:36.499
Its first paragraph becomes the summary you see

38
00:01:36.499 --> 00:01:37.916
in search.

39
00:01:38.636 --> 00:01:40.029
Add a package file,

40
00:01:40.029 --> 00:01:42.038
and it learns your frameworks.

41
00:01:42.038 --> 00:01:45.753
Add git, and it gains a history.

42
00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.133
Then run one command,

43
00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.654
right on your machine.

44
00:01:49.654 --> 00:01:51.013
Your new site appears,

45
00:01:51.013 --> 00:01:54.148
with its own article and its own colours.

46
00:01:55.268 --> 00:01:57.393
Want more of your machine in it?

47
00:01:57.427 --> 00:01:58.554
Add a root,

48
00:01:58.554 --> 00:02:01.085
and the crawl reaches further.

49
00:02:04.555 --> 00:02:07.040
Innernet is small and readable.

50
00:02:07.074 --> 00:02:08.781
One script writes the index,

51
00:02:08.781 --> 00:02:10.209
two libraries read it,

52
00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:12.345
and pages render on the server,

53
00:02:12.345 --> 00:02:15.759
behind a gate only this computer can open.

54
00:02:16.479 --> 00:02:18.035
A new search operator,

55
00:02:18.035 --> 00:02:19.265
a special page,

56
00:02:19.265 --> 00:02:21.309
a section on every article:

57
00:02:21.309 --> 00:02:24.293
each lives in one known place.

58
00:02:25.013 --> 00:02:26.406
Make the change.

59
00:02:26.406 --> 00:02:27.730
Check the types.

60
00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.169
Crawl the pages.

61
00:02:29.169 --> 00:02:30.713
Look at a screenshot.

62
00:02:30.713 --> 00:02:32.478
Open a pull request.

63
00:02:32.478 --> 00:02:34.371
And keep the one promise:

64
00:02:34.371 --> 00:02:36.867
everything stays local.

65
00:02:38.137 --> 00:02:40.366
Your folders were always a web.

66
00:02:40.366 --> 00:02:41.875
Now you can wander it:

67
00:02:41.875 --> 00:02:45.487
private, local, and yours.
